        "id": "request",
        "hash": "c7348ea9bff44e59286b4254fe587a83749dd4d201f346844dc90f4bbe167845",
        "text": "With default RunConfig, Gateway.call sends a valid Jev request for model \"typesafe/jev-1.13\". OpenRouter answers with model \"jev-1.13.2\" and otherwise valid usage, cost and answers. Would jev_decide.validate_response alone accept this model? What error code does the Gateway record for the call?"
      },
      {
        "id": "identity",
        "hash": "822ebc9bcd568768b93027cd1b46a53edbd8f77eeee01eef544844e288e74f15",
        "text": "    def _validate_identity(self, role, response, payload):\n        returned = response.get(\"model\")\n        require(isinstance(returned, str), \"missing_response_model\")\n        normalized = \"typesafe/\" + returned.removeprefix(\"typesafe/\") if role == \"jev\" else returned\n        require(normalized in self.config.response_models(role, payload[\"model\"]), \"response_model_mismatch\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "config",
        "hash": "0d8633d39ad3f3ffbdbfa067c3b1ba835fcb5f1656020c537c3c3516a1f06949",
        "text": "    jev_model: str = \"typesafe/jev-1.13\"\n    ...\n    jev_model_aliases: tuple = (\"typesafe/jev-1.13-20260917\",)\n    ...\n    def response_models(self, role, requested_model=None):\n        _require(role in (\"worker\", \"checker\", \"jev\"), \"invalid_role\")\n        if role == \"worker\" and requested_model is not None and requested_model != self.worker_model:\n            _require(any(route[\"model\"] == requested_model for route in self.worker_routes()),\n                     \"worker_model_not_permitted\")\n            return (requested_model,)\n        return (getattr(self, role + \"_model\"),) + getattr(self, role + \"_model_aliases\")"
      },
      {
        "id": "jev",
        "hash": "d1cfaa9a0e9588c7ab40fb09b86f6575596e4c91760576698c1750c91f57c5c0",
        "text": "    requested = request[\"model\"].removeprefix(\"~\").removeprefix(\"typesafe/\")\n    returned = response[\"model\"].removeprefix(\"typesafe/\")\n    require(re.fullmatch(r\"jev-[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\", returned) and\n            (requested == \"jev-latest\" or returned == requested or\n             returned.startswith((requested + \".\", requested + \"-\"))), \"response_model_mismatch\")"
      }
    ],
